    "ights 700 \xE2\x80\x94 hand-drawn narrow caps, has Cyrillic\\n- Press Start 2P \xE2\x80\x94 weights 400 \xE2\x80\x94 pixel / retro, has Cyrillic\\n- Lilita One \xE2\x80\x94 weights 400 \xE2\x80\x94 casual game display (Latin only)\\n- Luckiest Guy \xE2\x80\x94 weights 400 \xE2\x80\x94 cartoon caps (Latin only)\\n- Bangers \xE2\x80\x94 weights 400 \xE2\x80\x94 comic caps (Latin only)\\n\\nAnswer with JSON only, an object with these fields:\\n\\\"role\\\": \\\"title|heading|body|button|caption|number|label\\\", \\\"font\\\": \\\"<family from the list>\\\", \\\"weight\\\": <one of that font's weights>, \\\"size\\\": <px on a 1080-px-wide screen>,\\n\\\"color\\\": \\\"#RRGGBB\\\" \xE2\x80\x94 the fill when it is one flat colour (with a gradient: its first colour);\\n\\\"fill\\\": null for a flat fill, or a gradient {\\\"angle\\\": <degrees: 90 = top to bottom, 0 = left to right>, \\\"stops\\\": [{\\\"color\\\": \\\"#RRGGBB\\\", \\\"at\\\": <0..1>}, ...]} \xE2\x80\x94 2 to 6 stops from the start of the gradient to its end; two stops at the same \\\"at\\\" make a hard edge (a glossy band across the letters);\\n\\\"effects\\\": [...] \xE2\x80\x94 layer effects as in a Photoshop layer style, any number of each kind, at most 8 in all, [] for plain letters, the top layer first; sizes are px at that size:\\n  {\\\"type\\\": \\\"stroke\\\", \\\"color\\\": \\\"#RRGGBB\\\", \\\"width\\\": <px>, \\\"opacity\\\": <0..1>} \xE2\x80\x94 an outline outside the letters. Several strokes nest: the first is next to the letters, each next one goes around the previous (a thin light line, then a thick dark contour); an outline whose colour changes across it takes \\\"fill\\\": a gradient as above (then \\\"color\\\" is it",
    "s first colour);\\n  {\\\"type\\\": \\\"extrude\\\", \\\"color\\\": \\\"#RRGGBB\\\", \\\"x\\\": <px>, \\\"y\\\": <px>} \xE2\x80\x94 solid 3D depth: the outlined letters repeated towards the offset \xE2\x80\x94 the thick dark \\\"lip\\\" under cartoon titles and button labels;\\n  {\\\"type\\\": \\\"shadow\\\", \\\"color\\\": \\\"#RRGGBB\\\", \\\"x\\\": <px>, \\\"y\\\": <px>, \\\"blur\\\": <px>, \\\"spread\\\": <px>, \\\"opacity\\\": <0..1>} \xE2\x80\x94 a drop shadow of the whole outlined shape; blur 0 = a hard offset copy;\\n  {\\\"type\\\": \\\"glow\\\", \\\"color\\\": \\\"#RRGGBB\\\", \\\"size\\\": <px>, \\\"opacity\\\": <0..1>} \xE2\x80\x94 a soft halo around the shape;\\n  {\\\"type\\\": \\\"innerShadow\\\", \\\"color\\\": \\\"#RRGGBB\\\", \\\"x\\\": <px>, \\\"y\\\": <px>, \\\"blur\\\": <px>, \\\"opacity\\\": <0..1>} \xE2\x80\x94 a shade inside the letters along their edge: y > 0 darkens (or, with a light colour, lights) their top, y < 0 their bottom; x 0 and y 0 = an inner glow;\\n  {\\\"type\\\": \\\"bevel\\\", \\\"highlight\\\": \\\"#RRGGBB\\\", \\\"shade\\\": \\\"#RRGGBB\\\", \\\"depth\\\": <px>, \\\"soft\\\": <px>, \\\"opacity\\\": <0..1>} \xE2\x80\x94 a light edge inside the top of the letters and a dark one inside the bottom: embossed, volumetric letters.\\n\\\"letterSpacing\\\": <px>, \\\"lineHeight\\\": <multiple of size>, \\\"uppercase\\\": true|false, \\\"align\\\": \\\"left|center|right\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"<one sentence: where the style is used>\\\"\\n\\nRules: keep what the request does not ask to change \xE2\x80\x94 \\\"effects\\\" is the whole list, so repeat the effects that stay; effects scale with the size (a 100 px title takes a 6\xE2\x80\x93" "10 px outline); build rich looks out of several effects (a casua",
